<article class="env-lemma" id="075H">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/075H">Lemma <span data-tag="075H">96.21.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\tau \in \{ Zariski,\linebreak[0] {\acute{e}tale},\linebreak[0] smooth,\linebreak[0] syntomic,\linebreak[0] fppf\} $. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ \mathcal{Y}' \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X} \ar[r]_{g'} \ar[d]_{f'} &  \mathcal{X} \ar[d]^ f \\  \mathcal{Y}' \ar[r]^ g &  \mathcal{Y} }  \]
</div>
  <p> be a $2$-cartesian diagram of algebraic stacks over $S$. Then the base change map is an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  g^{-1}Rf_*\mathcal{F} \longrightarrow Rf'_*(g')^{-1}\mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
  <p> functorial for $\mathcal{F}$ in $\textit{Ab}(\mathcal{X}_\tau )$ or $\mathcal{F}$ in $\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{X}_\tau , \mathcal{O}_\mathcal {X})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The isomorphism $g^{-1}f_*\mathcal{F} = f'_*(g')^{-1}\mathcal{F}$ is Lemma <a href="/tag/075B" data-tag="075B">96.5.1</a> (and it holds for arbitrary presheaves). For the total direct images, there is a base change map because the morphisms $g$ and $g'$ are flat, see Cohomology on Sites, Section <a href="/tag/0735" data-tag="0735">21.15</a>. To see that this map is a quasi-isomorphism we can use that for an object $y'$ of $\mathcal{Y}'$ over a scheme $V$ there is an equivalence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (\mathit{Sch}/V)_{fppf} \times _{g(y'), \mathcal{Y}} \mathcal{X} = (\mathit{Sch}/V)_{fppf} \times _{y', \mathcal{Y}'} (\mathcal{Y}' \times _\mathcal {Y} \mathcal{X})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       We conclude that the induced map $g^{-1}R^ if_*\mathcal{F} \to R^ if'_*(g')^{-1}\mathcal{F}$ is an isomorphism by Lemma <a href="/tag/075G" data-tag="075G">96.21.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>